  "text": "To find the equation of the tangent line to the parabola at the point of intersection, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the point of intersection:**\n   The equation of the parabola is \\( y = x^2 \\) and the equation of the circle is \\( x^2 + y^2 - 4x - 4y - 5 = 0 \\).\n   \n   Substitute \\( y = x^2 \\) into the circle's equation:\n   \\[\n   x^2 + (x^2)^2 - 4x - 4x^2 - 5 = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplify this to:\n   \\[\n   x^4 - 3x^2 - 4x - 5 = 0\n   \\]\n   This is a quartic equation. We need to find a solution. Try rational roots using possible rational roots (±1, ±5, ±1/2, ±5/2).\n\n2. **Find the roots:**\n   Using the Rational Root Theorem, we test ±1:\n   \\[\n   (-1)^4 - 3(-1)^2 - 4(-1) - 5 = 1 - 3 + 4 - 5 = -3 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (1)^4 - 3(1)^2 - 4(1) - 5 = 1 - 3 - 4 - 5 = -11 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   Try ±5:\n   \\[\n   (5)^4 - 3(5)^2 - 4(5) - 5 = 625 - 75 - 20 - 5 = 525 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   Try ±1/2, ±5/2:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^4 - 3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 - 4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 5 = \\frac{1}{16} - \\frac{3}{4} - 2 - 5 = \\frac{1}{16} - \\frac{12}{16} - \\frac{32}{16} = -\\frac{43}{16} \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   Try ±5/2:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^4 - 3\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 - 4\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) - 5 = \\frac{625}{16} - \\frac{75}{4} - 10 - 5 = \\frac{625}{16} - \\frac{300}{16} - \\frac{160}{16} - \\frac{80}{16} = 0\n   \\]\n   So \\( x = \\frac{5}{2} \\) is a root.\n\n3. **Substitute back to find \\( y \\):**\n   \\[\n   y = \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{25}{4}\n   \\]\n   So the point of intersection is \\( \\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{25}{4}\\right) \\).\n\n4. **Find the slope of the tangent line:**\n   The derivative of \\( y = x^2 \\) is \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x \\).\n   At \\( x = \\frac{5}{2} \\), the slope is \\( 2 \\cdot \\frac{5}{2} = 5 \\).\n\n5. **Equation of the tangent line:**\n   The equation of a line with slope \\( m \\) passing through the point \\( (x_1, y_1) \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( m = 5 \\) and \\( (x_1, y_1) = \\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{25}{4}\\right) \\):\n   \\[\n   y - \\frac{25}{4} = 5(x - \\frac{5}{2})\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   y - \\frac{25}{4} = 5x - \\frac{25}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = 5x - \\frac{25}{2} + \\frac{25}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = 5x - \\frac{50}{4} + \\frac{25}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = 5x - \\frac{25}{4}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the equation of the tangent line is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{y = 5x - \\frac{25}{4}}\n   \\]",
